In Supabase SQL editor, remove the legacy NOT NULL columns from public.devices so the app's INSERT payload succeeds. Recommended:
  ALTER TABLE public.devices DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS device_name;
  ALTER TABLE public.devices DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS device_type;
  ALTER TABLE public.devices DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS device_uuid;
  -- (repeat for any other legacy columns the pg_catalog reveals)
  NOTIFY pgrst, 'reload schema';
  Alternatively, since the table has no data, safer/cleaner: DROP TABLE public.devices CASCADE; then re-run the CREATE TABLE public.devices … block from /app/supabase/schema.sql. CASCADE will also drop any dependent extra_time_requests rows, but there are none in this env.
